<info>
  <p>Share a selected tab in the URL with <code>Fez.url.hqs('tab', 'settings').push()</code>.</p>
  <p><code>Fez.url.qs()</code> and <code>Fez.url.pqs()</code> use the same interface for the query string and <code>/key:value</code> path params.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>push()</code> adds a history entry without fetching or scrolling.</li>
    <li><code>replace()</code> replaces the current entry.</li>
    <li><code>String(Fez.url.hqs('tab', 'x'))</code> returns the URL without changing it.</li>
    <li>Read with <code>Fez.url.hqs('tab')</code>; remove with <code>Fez.url.hqs('tab', null)</code>.</li>
    <li>Values are strings; missing keys return <code>undefined</code>.</li>
    <li>A slashless fragment with <code>=</code> is a parameter list, not an anchor ID or router path.</li>
    <li>Writes do not emit browser events. Update state after writing and listen for Back/Forward.</li>
    <li>Hash-only Back/Forward keeps the page mounted. Query or path changes use pjax navigation when active.</li>
  </ul>
</info>

<demo>
  <demo-hash-state />
</demo>

<script>
  class {
    init() {
      this.syncUrl()
    }

    onMount() {
      this.on('popstate', this.syncUrl)
      this.on('hashchange', this.syncUrl)
    }

    syncUrl() {
      this.state.tab = Fez.url.hqs('tab') || 'overview'
      this.state.url = location.pathname + location.search + location.hash
    }

    select(tab, replace = false) {
      const url = Fez.url.hqs('tab', tab)
      replace ? url.replace() : url.push()
      this.syncUrl()
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  display: block;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
  border-radius: 12px;

  nav, .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  button {
    padding: 8px 14px;
    border: 1px solid #94a3b8;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;

    &[aria-pressed="true"] {
      background: #1d4ed8;
      border-color: #1d4ed8;
      color: white;
    }
  }

  code {
    display: block;
    margin: 16px 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>

<nav aria-label="URL state tabs">
  <button type="button" aria-pressed={state.tab === 'overview' ? 'true' : 'false'} onclick="fez.select('overview')">Overview</button>
  <button type="button" aria-pressed={state.tab === 'settings' ? 'true' : 'false'} onclick="fez.select('settings')">Settings</button>
</nav>
<p aria-live="polite">Selected tab: <strong>{state.tab}</strong></p>
<code>{state.url}</code>
<div class="actions">
  <button type="button" onclick="fez.select('overview', true)">Replace with overview</button>
  <button type="button" onclick="fez.select(null)">Clear tab</button>
</div>
<p>Choose a tab, then use your browser's Back and Forward buttons.</p>
